  annote = {Verified 2026-10-09. Opened the V3 PDF and the current draft (rltheorybook_ABJKS.pdf, 27 June 2026, which adds K. Brantley as an author).
            Cite: simulation lemma = Lemma 2.2 (an identity: Q^pi - Q^pi_hat = gamma (I - gamma P_hat^pi)^-1 (P - P_hat) V^pi; the horizon factor follows);
            contraction = Lemma 1.10 (s1.3.1). Lemma 1.10 is the contraction of the OPTIMALITY operator on Q. Module 1's T^pi contraction is a one-line argument
            and needs no citation. Bellman optimality = Thm 1.8. Numbering is the same in both versions (academic-director review re-checked V3, 2022-01-31).
            Also opened (academic director, Module 1, 2026-10-10): Lemma 1.4 (Bellman consistency); Cor 1.5 (Q^pi = (I - gamma P^pi)^-1 r,
            with the infinity-norm invertibility argument); Thm 1.7 (a stationary deterministic optimal policy exists); Thm 1.8 (optimality
            equations for Q; the greedy policy w.r.t. Q* is optimal); Lemma 1.11 (greedy-policy loss: V^{pi_Q} >= V* - 2||Q - Q*||_inf/ (1 - gamma),
            no gamma in the numerator; Module 2 cites this).
            Also opened (academic director, Module 2, 2026-10-17, V3 PDF dated January 31, 2022, text extracted with pypdf): s1.1 (p. 5) r: S x A -> [0, 1];
            s1.3.1 (pp. 12-14) Lemma 1.10 (contraction of T on Q), Lemma 1.11 (Q-error amplification: V^{pi_Q} >= V* - 2||Q - Q*||_inf/(1 - gamma) 1),
            Theorem 1.12 (Q-value iteration convergence: k >= log(2/((1-gamma)^2 eps))/(1-gamma) gives V^{pi_k} >= V* - eps); s1.3.2 (pp. 14-15) policy
            iteration, Lemma 1.13 (Q^{pi_{k+1}} >= T Q^{pi_k} >= Q^{pi_k}; ||Q^{pi_{k+1}} - Q*||_inf <= gamma ||Q^{pi_k} - Q*||_inf), Theorem 1.14
            (policy iteration convergence: k >= log(1/((1-gamma) eps))/(1-gamma)), Table 0.1 (VI, PI, LP complexities); s1.6 attributes Lemma 1.11 to
            Singh and Yee [1994] (not opened; OPEN_QUESTIONS B27); s2.1 (pp. 21-23) generative model, P_hat = count/N, Proposition 2.1 (model accuracy,
            uniform value accuracy ||Q^pi - Q_hat^pi||_inf <= eps, near optimal planning ||Q^{pi_hat} - Q*||_inf <= 2 eps;
            the proof leaves this last inequality 'as an exercise to the reader', so Module 2 proves its state-value form itself), Lemma 2.2 (simulation lemma,
            reward known, rewards deterministic in chapter 2), Lemma 2.3 (||(I - gamma P^pi)^{-1} v||_inf <= ||v||_inf/(1 - gamma)); the proof of
            Proposition 2.1 bounds ||Q^pi - Q_hat^pi||_inf <= gamma/(1-gamma)^2 max_{s,a} ||P(.|s,a) - P_hat(.|s,a)||_1 and uses
            ||P(.|s,a) - P_hat(.|s,a)||_1 <= c sqrt(|S| log(1/delta)/m). Module 2 cites all of these.
            CAVEAT: the current draft is updated often, so cite V3.}
}

